IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp5-months`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II, Division D (Payment of Benefits: Special Rules Applicable)
-- DISABLED CONTRIBUTOR'S CHILD'S BENEFIT AND ORPHAN'S BENEFIT: sections 74, 75 and 76.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- A month is the DATE of its first day. Whether a child is a "dependent child", a "disabled contributor's child"
-- or an "orphan", and when a child ceases to be a dependent child, are defined in subsection 42(1) (piece cp3):
-- here they are plain facts. Regulation 65.1 (the Regulations, piece cr2) defines "maintaining the child" for
-- paragraph 76(1)(d); it is read in the rule for that paragraph, and cr2 encodes the regulation itself.

-- out of range: subsection 42(1) (piece cp3): "child", "dependent child", "disabled contributor's child", "orphan" and "parenting time", plain facts here
-- out of range: paragraphs 44(1)(e) and (f) (piece cp3): the entitlement to the benefit, assumed by the rules of this piece
-- out of range: section 60 (piece cp4): the application and the Minister's approval of payment
-- out of range: subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act (not among the texts read): "decision-making responsibility"
-- out of range: regulation 65.1 (piece cr2): read in s 76(1)(d)

§ `Part II, Division D -- Disabled contributor's child's benefit and orphan's benefit (sections 74 to 76)`

§§ `Subsection 74(1) -- who may apply`

-- src:2374 | Persons by whom application may be made
-- src:2375 | 74 (1) An application for a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit or orphan’s benefit may be made on behalf of a disabled contributor’s child or orphan by the child or orphan or by any other person or agency to whom the benefit would, if the application were approved, be payable under this Part.
@ref Act s 74(1) (src:2375)
GIVEN `the applicant is the child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a person or agency to whom the benefit would be payable if the application were approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 74(1) — the application may be made on behalf of the disabled contributor's child or orphan by the applicant` `the applicant is the child or orphan` `the applicant is a person or agency to whom the benefit would be payable if the application were approved` MEANS
        `the applicant is the child or orphan`
     OR `the applicant is a person or agency to whom the benefit would be payable if the application were approved`

§§ `Subsection 74(2) -- when payment begins`

-- src:2376 | Commencement of payment of benefit
-- src:2377 | (2) Subject to section 62, where payment of a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit or orphan’s benefit in respect of a contributor is approved, the benefit is payable for each month commencing with,
-- src:2378 | (a) in the case of a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit, the later of
-- src:2379 | (i) the month commencing with which a disability pension is payable to the contributor under this Act or under a provincial pension plan or a post-retirement disability benefit is payable under this Act, and
-- src:2380 | (ii) the month next following the month in which the child was born or otherwise became a child of the contributor, and
-- src:2381 | (b) in the case of an orphan’s benefit, the later of
-- src:2382 | (i) the month following the month in which the contributor died, and
-- src:2383 | (ii) the month next following the month in which the child was born,
-- src:2384 | but in no case earlier than the twelfth month preceding the month following the month in which the application was received.
@ref Act s 74(2)(a) (src:2377-2381)
-- The earliest month the application allows: "in no case earlier than the twelfth month preceding the month following
-- the month in which the application was received".
GIVEN `a day in the month the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 74(2) — the earliest month for which a benefit is payable, by reason of the application` `a day in the month the application was received` MEANS
    `cp5 helper -- the month a number of months from the month of a date` `a day in the month the application was received` (0 MINUS 11)

@ref Act s 74(2)(a) (src:2378-2380)
GIVEN `payment of the disabled contributor's child's benefit is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first month for which a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month the child was born or otherwise became a child of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 74(2)(a) — the first month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` `payment of the disabled contributor's child's benefit is approved` `first month for which a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` `a day in the month the child was born or otherwise became a child of the contributor` `a day in the month the application was received` MEANS
    IF NOT `payment of the disabled contributor's child's benefit is approved`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`cp5 helper -- the later of two days` fromContributorOrChild earliest)
    WHERE
        -- the later of (i) the month commencing with which a disability pension (or post-retirement disability benefit) is payable
        -- to the contributor and (ii) the month next following the month in which the child was born or otherwise became a child of the contributor
        fromContributorOrChild MEANS `cp5 helper -- the later of two days` `first month for which a disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is payable to the contributor` (`the month following the month of a date` `a day in the month the child was born or otherwise became a child of the contributor`)
        earliest MEANS `s 74(2) — the earliest month for which a benefit is payable, by reason of the application` `a day in the month the application was received`

@ref Act s 74(2)(b) (src:2381-2384)
GIVEN `payment of the orphan's benefit is approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month the contributor died` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month the child was born` IS A DATE
      `a day in the month the application was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 74(2)(b) — the first month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` `payment of the orphan's benefit is approved` `a day in the month the contributor died` `a day in the month the child was born` `a day in the month the application was received` MEANS
    IF NOT `payment of the orphan's benefit is approved`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`cp5 helper -- the later of two days` fromDeathOrBirth earliest)
    WHERE
        -- the later of (i) the month following the month in which the contributor died and (ii) the month next following the month in which the child was born
        fromDeathOrBirth MEANS `cp5 helper -- the later of two days` (`the month following the month of a date` `a day in the month the contributor died`) (`the month following the month of a date` `a day in the month the child was born`)
        earliest MEANS `s 74(2) — the earliest month for which a benefit is payable, by reason of the application` `a day in the month the application was received`

§§ `Subsections 74(3) and (3.1) -- no benefit in respect of more than two contributors`

-- src:2387 | Meaning of parent
-- src:2388 | (3.1) In subsection (3), parent has the reciprocal meaning to that of “child”.
@ref Act s 74(3.1) (src:2388)
GIVEN `the child is a child of the person within the meaning of the definition child of a contributor in subsection 42(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 74(3.1) — the person is a parent of the child` `the child is a child of the person within the meaning of the definition child of a contributor in subsection 42(1)` MEANS
    `the child is a child of the person within the meaning of the definition child of a contributor in subsection 42(1)`

-- src:2385 | No benefit in respect of more than two contributors
-- src:2386 | (3) Where a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit has become payable to a child under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in respect of any contributor thereunder or an orphan’s benefit has become payable to an orphan under this Act or under a provincial pension plan in respect of any contributor thereunder, no disabled contributor’s child’s benefit or orphan’s benefit is payable to that person under this Act in respect of any other such contributor except another parent of that person, and in no case shall such a benefit be paid to that person in respect of more than two contributors.
@ref Act s 74(3) (src:2386)
GIVEN `a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit has become payable to the person in respect of another contributor under this Act or a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor is a parent of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of contributors in respect of whom such a benefit has been paid to the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 74(3) — the benefit is not payable to the person in respect of the contributor` `a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit has become payable to the person in respect of another contributor under this Act or a provincial pension plan` `the contributor is a parent of the person` `the number of contributors in respect of whom such a benefit has been paid to the person` MEANS
    -- no benefit in respect of any other contributor except another parent of that person
        (   `a disabled contributor's child's benefit or an orphan's benefit has become payable to the person in respect of another contributor under this Act or a provincial pension plan`
        AND (NOT `the contributor is a parent of the person`))
    -- and in no case in respect of more than two contributors
     OR `the number of contributors in respect of whom such a benefit has been paid to the person` AT LEAST 2

§§ `Section 75 -- to whom the benefit is paid`

-- src:2390 | Payment of benefit
-- src:2391 | 75 (1) If a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit is payable to a child of a disabled contributor or an orphan’s benefit is payable to an orphan of a contributor and the child or orphan has not reached 18 years of age, payment of the benefit must be made to the person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan, or, if there is no person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan, to any person or agency that the Minister may direct.
@ref Act s 75(1) (src:2391)
DECLARE `cp5 Payee of a child's or orphan's benefit` IS ONE OF
    `the benefit is paid to the person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan`
    `the benefit is paid to the person or agency the Minister directs`

@ref Act s 75(1) (src:2391)
GIVEN `date of birth of the child or orphan` IS A DATE
      `day as at which the payee is decided` IS A DATE
      `there is a person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `cp5 Payee of a child's or orphan's benefit`
`s 75(1) — to whom a disabled contributor's child's benefit or orphan's benefit is paid` `date of birth of the child or orphan` `day as at which the payee is decided` `there is a person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` MEANS
    IF `cp5 helper -- the person has reached an age on a day under section 2(2)` `date of birth of the child or orphan` 18 `day as at which the payee is decided`
    -- the subsection speaks only of a child or orphan who has not reached 18: for one who has, the text of this range does not say (NOTES.md, fork F24)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `there is a person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan`
         THEN JUST `the benefit is paid to the person or agency having decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan`
         ELSE JUST `the benefit is paid to the person or agency the Minister directs`

-- src:2392 | Presumption — decision-making responsibility
-- src:2393 | (2) For the purposes of this Part, in the absence of any evidence to the contrary, the following person is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan, as the case may be:
-- src:2394 | (a) the contributor, in relation to a disabled contributor’s child, except if the contributor has less than 20% of the parenting time in respect of the child; and
-- src:2395 | (b) the survivor, if any, of the contributor, in relation to an orphan, except if the survivor has less than 20% of the parenting time in respect of the orphan.
@ref Act s 75(2) (src:2393-2395)
DECLARE `cp5 Person presumed to have decision-making responsibility` IS ONE OF
    `the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child`
    `the survivor of the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the orphan`
    `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`

-- out of range: the meaning of "decision-making responsibility" (subsection 2(1) of the Divorce Act, not an input) and of
-- "parenting time" (subsection 42(1), piece cp3). The share of the parenting time is a plain number, a percentage.
@ref Act s 75(2) (src:2393-2395)
GIVEN `the benefit is an orphan's benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a survivor of the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage of the parenting time that the contributor or survivor has` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `cp5 Person presumed to have decision-making responsibility`
`s 75(2) — the person presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child or orphan` `the benefit is an orphan's benefit` `there is evidence to the contrary` `there is a survivor of the contributor` `the percentage of the parenting time that the contributor or survivor has` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary` THEN `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`
        IF `the benefit is an orphan's benefit`
           THEN (IF `there is a survivor of the contributor` AND (NOT (`the percentage of the parenting time that the contributor or survivor has` BELOW 20))
                 THEN `the survivor of the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the orphan`
                 ELSE `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`)
        OTHERWISE (IF `the percentage of the parenting time that the contributor or survivor has` BELOW 20
                   THEN `no one is presumed to have decision-making responsibility under subsection 75(2)`
                   ELSE `the contributor is presumed to have decision-making responsibility for the child`)

§§ `Section 76 -- when the benefit ceases to be payable`

-- Regulation 65.1(b) (the Regulations, piece cr2): "maintaining the child", for the child of a disabled contributor,
-- means making periodically, for the child, financial provision amounting to not less than the disabled contributor's
-- child's benefit payable under the Act.
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:649 | 65.1 For the purposes of subsection 42(1) and paragraph 76(1)(d) of the Act, maintaining the child
-- src:C.R.C.-c.-385:651 | (b) with reference to the child of a disabled contributor, means making periodically, for the child, financial provision amounting to not less than the disabled contributor’s child’s benefit payable under the Act.
@ref Reg 65.1 (src:C.R.C.-c.-385:649-651)
GIVEN `the contributor makes financial provision for the child periodically` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the periodic provision for the child` IS A NUMBER
      `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76(1)(d) — the disabled contributor is maintaining the child, as defined by regulation 65.1(b)` `the contributor makes financial provision for the child periodically` `the amount of the periodic provision for the child` `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act` MEANS
        `the contributor makes financial provision for the child periodically`
    AND `the amount of the periodic provision for the child` AT LEAST `the disabled contributor's child's benefit payable under the Act`

-- src:2396 | When disabled contributor’s child’s benefit ceases to be payable
-- src:2397 | 76 (1) A disabled contributor’s child’s benefit ceases to be payable with the payment for the month in which
-- src:2398 | (a) the child ceases to be a dependent child;
-- src:2399 | (b) the child dies;
-- src:2400 | (c) the contributor’s disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceases to be payable for any reason other than that the contributor has reached 65 years of age;
-- src:2401 | (d) the child is adopted legally or in fact by someone other than the disabled contributor or the disabled contributor’s spouse or common-law partner, unless the disabled contributor is maintaining the child, as defined by regulation; or
-- src:2402 | (e) the disabled contributor ceases to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the child, if the child is a child as defined in subsection 42(1) by reason of the disabled contributor having had that parenting time or decision-making responsibility.
@ref Act s 76(1) (src:2397-2402)
GIVEN `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a day in the month the child died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a day in the month the contributor's disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased to be payable for a reason other than that the contributor reached 65` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a day in the month the child was adopted by someone other than the disabled contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the disabled contributor is maintaining the child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a day in the month the disabled contributor ceased to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the child` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the child is a child as defined in subsection 42(1) by reason of the contributor having had that parenting time or decision-making responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76(1) — the last month for which a disabled contributor's child's benefit is payable` `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child` `a day in the month the child died` `a day in the month the contributor's disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased to be payable for a reason other than that the contributor reached 65` `a day in the month the child was adopted by someone other than the disabled contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner` `the disabled contributor is maintaining the child` `a day in the month the disabled contributor ceased to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the child` `the child is a child as defined in subsection 42(1) by reason of the contributor having had that parenting time or decision-making responsibility` MEANS
    `cp5 helper -- the earliest of the months that apply` (LIST
        -- (a) the child ceases to be a dependent child
        `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child`,
        -- (b) the child dies
        `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `a day in the month the child died`,
        -- (c) the contributor's disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceases to be payable for any reason other than reaching 65
        `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `a day in the month the contributor's disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit ceased to be payable for a reason other than that the contributor reached 65`,
        -- (d) the child is adopted by someone other than the contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner, unless the contributor is maintaining the child
        IF `the disabled contributor is maintaining the child` THEN NOTHING ELSE `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `a day in the month the child was adopted by someone other than the disabled contributor or the contributor's spouse or common-law partner`,
        -- (e) the contributor ceases to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility, if the child is a child by reason of having had it
        IF `the child is a child as defined in subsection 42(1) by reason of the contributor having had that parenting time or decision-making responsibility` THEN `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `a day in the month the disabled contributor ceased to have parenting time or decision-making responsibility in respect of the child` ELSE NOTHING)

-- src:2403 | When orphan’s benefit ceases to be payable
-- src:2404 | (2) An orphan’s benefit ceases to be payable with the payment for the month in which the child ceases to be a dependent child or dies.
@ref Act s 76(2) (src:2404)
GIVEN `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a day in the month the child died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76(2) — the last month for which an orphan's benefit is payable` `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child` `a day in the month the child died` MEANS
    `cp5 helper -- the earliest of the months that apply` (LIST
        `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `a day in the month the child ceased to be a dependent child`,
        `cp5 helper -- the month of a date that may be absent` `a day in the month the child died`)

-- src:2405 | Exception
-- src:2406 | (3) Where, by reason of the death of a contributor, a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit ceases to be payable to a person who is 18 years of age or older at the time of that death, an application under section 60 for an orphan’s benefit shall be deemed to have been made by that person in the month in which the contributor died.
@ref Act s 76(3) (src:2406)
GIVEN `a disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases to be payable to the person by reason of the death of a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of birth of the person` IS A DATE
      `day the contributor died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76(3) — the month in which an application for an orphan's benefit is deemed made by the person` `a disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases to be payable to the person by reason of the death of a contributor` `date of birth of the person` `day the contributor died` MEANS
    IF     `a disabled contributor's child's benefit ceases to be payable to the person by reason of the death of a contributor`
       AND `cp5 helper -- the person has reached an age on a day under section 2(2)` `date of birth of the person` 18 `day the contributor died`
    THEN JUST (`the month of a date` `day the contributor died`)
    ELSE NOTHING
